WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.430
There's a trade war going
on between America and China

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.430
which is dominating global politics

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.100
and a lot of that has to do
with more traditional goods

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.980
like cars or soy beans.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.410
But actually quite all
of the attention is being

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.400
paid to semiconductors as well.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.370
So, semiconductors are a vital ingredient

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.530
in computer chips.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.860
They have electrical characteristics

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.360
that make the chips work.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.270
If you look in your car
you'll find not just one

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.560
but probably dozens of
different computers,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.200
your smart phone obviously in your pocket,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.070
whenever you do anything with your bank

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.410
that transaction will almost certainly

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.200
be handled electronically.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.930
They're only going to become more common

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.650
as computers spread further
and further into modern life.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.560
America is really the dominant player.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.610
Of the top 15 biggest companies
none of them are Chinese.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.760
China does have an industry

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.320
but a lot of it is dependent on imports

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.050
so semiconductor imports are
actually cost it more than oil.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.890
A lot of what it imports are components

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.440
that then go in to finished goods.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.850
So you think of things like your iPhone

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.370
which is assembled in China

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.810
but all of the designs for the chips

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.960
and the chips themselves
come from outside.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.740
Semiconductors are important
really for two reasons.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.440
One is economic and
they underlie huge parts

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.940
of the global economy so the
entire E-commerce industry,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.090
for instance, which have revenues

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.870
of that two trillion dollars a year,

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.850
would be impossible
without semiconductors.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.570
There's also a national security angle.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:17.610
In America, in particular,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.450
has always seen it's
lead in this technology

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.000
as a vital national security asset.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.260
And America's military was
actually one of the earliest

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.470
and biggest customers
for Silicon Valley chips.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.269
Even these days armies,
like everything else,

00:01:29.269 --> 00:01:31.230
are becoming increasingly digital

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.680
and semiconductors are
vital to make that happen.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.500
In order to build up
it's domestic industry,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.490
China's willing to spend a lot of money

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.300
so it's established an investment fund

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.047
designed to boost the local industry

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:48.150
and that it's capitalized that
with a 150 billion dollars.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.420
It's made semiconductors
one of the priority areas

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.950
in it's Made in China 2025 initiative

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.560
which is a general attempt
to boost manufacturing

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.950
across the country.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.330
America sees semiconductors
as a strategic good

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.140
so it's quite worried by China's attempts

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.530
to build up a domestic industry.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.260
Earlier this year America
forbade it's companies

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.090
from selling chips and
intellectual property to ZTE

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.900
which is a Chinese maker of smartphones

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.090
and telecom equipment.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.890
And because it's dependent
on American chips

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.190
the company was pushed to
the brink of bankruptcy

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.730
almost over night and was
only saved at the last minute

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.100
when Trump decided to rescind the ban.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.190
The ZTE affair proved two things.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.290
One, was that America's technological lead

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.900
translates in to political power.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.740
It can use this lead to
frustrate Chinese ambitions

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.630
but it also made it very clear to China

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.580
just how dependent their
companies are on American product.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:37.693
There are several ways

00:02:37.693 --> 00:02:40.650
in which America could respond to this.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.390
The first might be to try
and work with it's allies.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.600
Countries like South Korea, Japan, Taiwan

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.570
which have big chip manufacturing
industries of their own.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.940
To make sure that China doesn't
get an unnecessary leg up

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.210
but also to try and work
to establish standards

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.660
so that both sides can start
to trust each others products

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.493
a little bit more.

00:02:57.493 --> 00:02:59.330
A second idea is innovation,

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.670
is to try to push the
cutting edge out further,

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.990
to run faster to stay
ahead of China in the race

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.580
rather than trying to hobble the Chinese.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.680
But I think the final thing
America should do, as well,

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.830
is just to prepare for
a world in which China

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.470
is more overpowering in this industry

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.700
and does have more of an influence
over the digital economy.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.410
I think it can probably
try to slow China down.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:20.697
I'm not sure that it
can prevent it entirely

00:03:20.697 --> 00:03:21.910
and of course trying to do that

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.600
would be quite an aggressive move

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.730
that would also do quite a
lot of damage potentially

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.430
to a really vital industry

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.480
that underpins the entire global economy.

